{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical uncertainty for a multimodal study is whether image data carries useful signal for this task at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-only baseline under the same profile setting as config_001, allowing a clean modality comparison. If image-only substantially outperforms or underperforms RNA-only, it immediately tells us whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing and which modality dominates. If performance is similar, it suggests complementary signals that fusion could exploit. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty (is image informative?) before committing budget to the many multimodal configurations, making it the highest-information next step."
}

